<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49329" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">trŭtĭno</span></b> ,
			āre, 1, v. a., and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">trŭtĭnor</span></b> ,
			ātus, 1, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. dep. a.</i> [trutina] </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Dep.</i> form, <i>to weigh</i>, <i>balance</i> (syn. pensito).—<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">verba,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Pers.
					3, 82</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Act.</i>, <i><span class="en">Hier. Ep. 36,
			14</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">diu trutinandus est, cui traduntur examina,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cassiod. Var. 5, 40</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">trŭtĭnā-tus</span></b> , a,
				um, in a <i>pass.</i> signif.,
					<i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 7, 9</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
